Expected elements: present

Identity bar with chain exit, hash, `Partial`, both step directions, scrubber, `128 / 1315`, phase rail; Code positioned at line 32; Call Trace/Event Log in one tab strip, Call Trace open; Values its own pane; Transaction pane opening with `DATA`, badge and producer's sentences. No band, no spinner.

This is a designed light theme, not an inverted dark one: a coherent neutral ladder (#ffffff / #ececeb / #dddddd / #a2a2a2), four text levels (#101010 / #242424 / #484848 / #565656) all above 6.7:1, and a light-native editor palette — #166534 comments, #6d28d9 numerals, #713f12 calls — none below 5.6:1. Nothing on the page is unreadable.

The roles are where it slips. `Synthetic demo data` and the active `FETCHING` pill are the same two tokens, #dbeafe on #1e40af: one colour meaning both "this is not real data" and "the engine is doing this now". The cyan family carries four meanings in four shades — #a5f3fc position band, #164e63 position rail, #0e7490 the new ran-rail and `⊙`, #155e75 scrubber — and on line 32 three of them stack inside 8px, so the new "this arm ran" mark is the same hue as "you are here", drawn on top of "you are here". Its counterpart `⊘` is plain body grey at 9.15:1 while `⊙` sits at 4.29:1; the accent went to the unremarkable state.

Fixes: give provenance a blue the loading phases do not use; take the ran-rail out of the position hue.

Rating: 6/10

